    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Once dubbed Sydney’s ‘little Italy’, Leichhardt’s Italian heritage has mellowed over the decades.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leichhardt%2C_New_South_Wales"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Leichhardt Town Hall, built in 1888, and the former Fire Station are prized examples of the suburb’s heritage architecture.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://leichhardt.nsw.guide/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Every October, Norton Street bursts into celebration during the Italian Fiesta, spotlighting the area’s enduring Italian culture.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leichhardt%2C_New_South_Wales"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Public School Buildings on Marion Street, first erected in 1891 and rebuilt in 1897, reflect Leichhardt’s long educational heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leichhardt%2C_New_South_Wales"
    },
    {
